## Story Description
Add rule method rule_spend_concentration_risk() to RecommendationRules in src/recommendations/rules.py. Fires when a L2 category has more than one supplier AND the top supplier holds more than cfg.concentration_threshold_pct (default 0.80) of category spend AND category_spend > cfg.competitive_tender_min_spend. The saving represents the risk mitigation cost of establishing a second source. n_suppliers must be > 1 to avoid overlap with COMPETITIVE_TENDER (which fires on exactly 1 supplier).

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: src/recommendations/rules.py — add constant at the top with other constants: SPEND_CONCENTRATION_RISK = 'SPEND_CONCENTRATION_RISK'
- Edit file: src/recommendations/rules.py — add rule_spend_concentration_risk() method to RecommendationRules class with this logic: (1) get txn from self.cube.get('transactions', pd.DataFrame()); check required columns {'category_l2', 'canonical_supplier_id', 'base_amount'} are all in txn.columns; (2) addr = self._addressable(txn); addr_cat = addr.dropna(subset=['category_l2']); (3) for category, group in addr_cat.groupby('category_l2'): n_suppliers = int(group['canonical_supplier_id'].nunique()); skip if n_suppliers <= 1; category_spend = float(group['base_amount'].sum()); skip if category_spend <= cfg.competitive_tender_min_spend; supplier_spend = group.groupby('canonical_supplier_id')['base_amount'].sum(); top_supplier_pct = float(supplier_spend.max() / category_spend); skip if top_supplier_pct <= cfg.concentration_threshold_pct; get top_supplier_id = supplier_spend.idxmax(); get top_supplier_name from group where canonical_supplier_id == top_supplier_id using canonical_supplier_name column if present; rates_row = self._rates.get(SPEND_CONCENTRATION_RISK, str(category)); saving_pct = rates_row['saving_pct']; addressability_pct = rates_row['addressability_pct']; addressable_baseline = category_spend * addressability_pct; estimated_impact = addressable_baseline * saving_pct; append dict with all required fields
- Edit file: src/recommendations/rules.py — the recommendation dict for SPEND_CONCENTRATION_RISK must include: type=SPEND_CONCENTRATION_RISK, context=str(category), evidence=f'{top_supplier_pct:.0%} of {category} spend concentrated in {top_supplier_name}; {n_suppliers} total suppliers; {addressability_pct:.0%} addressable', confidence='MEDIUM', action=f'Introduce second-source competition in {category} — {top_supplier_name} holds {top_supplier_pct:.0%} of spend', lever='Supply Risk Management', baseline_spend=round(category_spend, 2), addressability_pct=addressability_pct, saving_pct=saving_pct, addressable_baseline=round(addressable_baseline, 2)
- Edit file: src/recommendations/rules.py — add self.rule_spend_concentration_risk to rule_methods list in generate_all()
- Run: python -c "from src.recommendations.rules import SPEND_CONCENTRATION_RISK; print(SPEND_CONCENTRATION_RISK)" — should print SPEND_CONCENTRATION_RISK without error

